    * {
      font-family: 'Inter', Helvetica;
    }
  </style></head><body style="background-color:#FAF7F2;font-family:Inter, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;margin:0;padding:0"><!--$--><!--html--><!--head--><div style="display:none;overflow:hidden;line-height:1px;opacity:0;max-height:0;max-width:0">Invoices out, payments in, purchase orders tracked — one sheet each.<div> ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿</div></div><!--body--><table align="center" width="100%" border="0" cellPadding="0" cellSpacing="0" role="presentation" style="max-width:600px;margin:0 auto;background-color:#FFFFFF"><tbody><tr style="width:100%"><td><table align="center" width="100%" border="0" cellPadding="0" cellSpacing="0" role="presentation" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg, #C4A57B, #8B7355);padding:32px 40px;text-align:center"><tbody><tr><td><p style="font-size:28px;line-height:24px;margin:0;color:#FFFFFF;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px">Patina</p></td></tr></tbody></table><table align="center" width="100%" border="0" cellPadding="0" cellSpacing="0" role="presentation" style="padding:40px"><tbody><tr><td><p style="font-size:15px;line-height:25px;margin:0 0 18px 0;color:#4A453F">{{first_name}}<!-- -->,</p><p style="font-size:15px;line-height:25px;margin:0 0 18px 0;color:#4A453F">Once work is signed, the money has its own quiet order.</p><p style="font-size:15px;line-height:25px;margin:0 0 18px 0;color:#4A453F">Accounts is one sheet. A signed proposal becomes a deposit invoice in about two minutes — the numbers are already there. Your receivables sit in one view: what&#x27;s out, what&#x27;s paid, what&#x27;s late. Reminders go out on their own, so you are not the one nagging a client about a balance.</p><p style="font-size:15px;line-height:25px;margin:0 0 18px 0;color:#4A453F">Orders is the other sheet. Every purchase order carries its maker, its dates, and its status, so “where&#x27;s the credenza” has an answer you can read off a screen instead of chasing down a workshop.</p><p style="font-size:15px;line-height:25px;margin:0 0 18px 0;color:#4A453F">Both sheets slide over the document when you need them and slide back when you&#x27;re done. The ledgers serve the work — the work never bends to the ledgers.</p><p style="font-size:15px;line-height:25px;margin:0 0 18px 0;color:#4A453F">If anything of yours is signed, send the deposit invoice today. It&#x27;s the shortest path from yes to money in.</p><div style="margin:30px 0;text-align:center"><a href="{{app_url}}/desk?sheet=accounts" style="line-height:20px;text-decoration:none;display:inline-block;max-width:100%;mso-padding-alt:0px;border-radius:24px;font-size:15px;font-weight:600;text-align:center;padding:14px 32px 14px 32px;min-height:48px;background-color:#C4A57B;color:#FFFFFF" target="_blank"><span><!--[if mso]><i style="mso-font-width:400%;mso-text-raise:21" hidden>&#8202;&#8202;&#8202;&#8202;</i><![endif]--></span><span style="max-width:100%;display:inline-block;line-height:120%;mso-padding-alt:0px;mso-text-raise:10.5px">Open Accounts</span><span><!--[if mso]><i style="mso-font-width:400%" hidden>&#8202;&#8202;&#8202;&#8202;&#8203;</i><![endif]--></span></a></div><p style="font-size:15px;line-height:24px;margin:26px 0 0 0;color:#2C2926">— Kody</p></td></tr></tbody></table><table align="center" width="100%" border="0" cellPadding="0" cellSpacing="0" role="presentation" style="background-color:#2C2926;padding:32px 40px"><tbody><tr><td><hr style="width:100%;border:none;border-top:1px solid #eaeaea;border-color:#4A453F;margin:0 0 24px 0"/><p style="font-size:13px;line-height:20px;margin:0 0 8px 0;color:#A09890;text-align:center">Patina — Furniture intelligence for design professionals</p><p style="font-size:11px;line-height:16px;margin:0 0 12px 0;color:#7A736C;text-align:center">Patina Inc. · 123 Design Way, Suite 100 · San Francisco, CA 94102</p></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table><!--/$--></body></html>$html$, $html$["first_name"]$html$::jsonb, true),
  ($html$onboarding-aesthete$html$, $html$Onboarding: Aesthete (E9)$html$, $html$Day-30 spine email -- teaching Aesthete taste. Never skipped.$html$, $html$sequence$html$::email_template_category, $html$Teach it your taste$html$, $html$<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Transitional//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd"><html dir="ltr" lang="en"><head><meta content="text/html; charset=UTF-8" http-equiv="Content-Type"/><meta name="x-apple-disable-message-reformatting"/><style>
    @font-face {
